# Context boundary for the Cursor agent. Gitignore syntax.
#
# WHAT THIS ACTUALLY BLOCKS -- and, more importantly, what it does not.
#
# Blocked:   Agent, Tab, Inline Edit, @-mentions, and codebase indexing.
# NOT blocked: the terminal, and MCP tools.
#
# That second line is Cursor's documented behaviour, not a bug and not a
# surprise -- but it means .cursorignore alone is an incomplete control. An
# agent that cannot read handoff.md with the Read tool can still `cat` it. If
# the boundary has to hold, .cursorignore is layer one and a
# `beforeShellExecution` hook with "failClosed": true is layer two.
#
# We are treating that as load-bearing here for a specific reason. This project
# already shipped a tool whose docstring said "read-only" and which created
# topics on a live broker (handoff §14). The lesson written down at the time was
# that a safety property asserted in prose and never asserted in code is not a
# safety property. Trusting .cursorignore to block a `cat` would be the same
# mistake with a different filename.
#
# Use .cursorindexingignore instead when you want a file excluded from the index
# but still available to @-mention deliberately.

# --- must never leave this machine -----------------------------------------
# Contains EC2 hostnames, the SSH key path, and a plain-text note that the PROD
# broker has no auth. Not in git, not in the index, not in agent context.
handoff.md
*.pem
*.key

# --- unrelated work in the same parent directory ----------------------------
# Not secret, just noise -- indexing it would dilute retrieval on every query.
telco-platform-demo/

# --- generated, and holds live consumer-group offsets ------------------------
# Written by the promote workflow on the runner. Real group/partition/offset
# triples from PROD; there is no reason for an agent to read them and a good
# reason not to index them.
docs/changes/

# --- generated, high-volume, zero signal ------------------------------------
.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.airflow-home/
node_modules/

# --- artifacts -------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
.DS_Store

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   .cursor/rules/**  and  docs/RULES.md   are generated but MUST stay visible --
#   they are the agent's own context, and gen_rules.py --check is what keeps
#   them honest. Ignoring generated files by reflex would blind the agent to
#   the rules it is supposed to follow.

# Captured broker state for repeat rehearsals (tools/reset_demo.sh). Live
# consumer-group offsets -- same reason docs/changes/ is here.
baselines/
